# Who has to look before a change lands.
#
# design/requirements.md section 4.6 asks for a review gate on the facts file
# and on anything a reader is told to trust, and AGENTS.md rule 4 is the reason:
# an observed value is not a verified value. A drift run reports that a
# certificate or a hostname is not what the page says. Turning that report into
# a documented value is a judgement somebody makes out of band, so nothing here
# may reach main without a person on it.
#
# Today that person is one person, which makes most of this file a formality.
# It is written by path anyway, so the rule survives the second maintainer
# rather than being invented at the moment it is first needed. GitHub also
# refuses auto-merge on an owned path, which is the part that works today.

*                       @hutzelmann

# Documented values. Every page, every script and every check reads these, so a
# wrong one is wrong everywhere at once.
/facts/                 @hutzelmann

# Trust material in prose: certificate authorities, fingerprints, the bundle a
# reader is told to build.
/content/en/vpn/        @hutzelmann
/content/de/vpn/        @hutzelmann
/content/en/wifi/       @hutzelmann
/content/de/wifi/       @hutzelmann

# What the checks look at, and what runs them unattended.
/scripts/ci/            @hutzelmann
/.github/workflows/     @hutzelmann

# The contract the rest of this is enforced against.
/AGENTS.md              @hutzelmann
/.github/CODEOWNERS     @hutzelmann
